While playing Nethack yesterday, I noticed something strange.

My barbarian was wandering around on dungeon level 14 and happened
across a beehive.  Being a rather brave, albeit foolish barbarian,
I decided to take on all the killer bees at once - a mere 10 or 15 of them.

Well, I noticed something strange just as I started hacking them to pieces:

They didn't move :-)  The bees just sat there whilst I shredded them
with my two-handed sword.  Any reason in particular that they didn't move
at all?  Were they sleeping?  I would have thought that hacking up a few
of their brethern would have woken them up.

The same thing occasionally happens in throne rooms.  The only monster
that seems to fight back, is the one that I am currently attacking.  Even
though I am surrounded by monsters, only one will attack at a time.

Strange?  I thought so.  Makes taking on rooms full of monsters fairly easy.
This only happens about 60% of the time though.  Other times everything
seems to be 'normal'.

I'm running Nethack 3.0j on a MSDOS machine.


